From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ARMDeck <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:45:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle: wait longer
 for the source capabilities

The GameSir X3 Pro is a controller with a USB-C pass-through charging
port. When a charger is plugged into it, it takes over the power supply
from the phone with a power role swap, and after its PS_RDY it sends its
Source_Capabilities 337 ms later (measured on a OnePlus 8 on 2026-10-04).
tcpm waits only PD_T_SINK_WAIT_CAP, 310 ms, the lower end of the
310-620 ms range USB PD gives for tTypeCSinkWaitCap, and then sends a
hard reset. After that reset the phone stayed a USB device and the
pass-through charging did not work.

Set sink-wait-cap-time-ms to 620 ms, the upper end of the range in the
USB PD specification and in the usb-connector binding. The OnePlus PD
stack on Android waits 500 ms (SINK_WAIT_CAP_TIME in
drivers/usb/pd/policy_engine.c of the vendor kernel), which also covers
the 337 ms; 620 ms leaves more margin for slower sources. Only this
timeout changes, no voltage or current limit.

Tested on a OnePlus 8 (IN2013) on 2026-10-04 with the same property added
to the DTB through fdtput (test image r8w): the X3 Pro takes over the
supply without a hard reset and pass-through charging works.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts
index 53773b5..c61d01e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts
@@ -1298,6 +1298,15 @@
 				       PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM |
 				       PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
 
+		/*
+		 * Wait up to 620 ms (the USB PD maximum) for the source's
+		 * capabilities: after a power role swap the GameSir X3 Pro sends
+		 * them 337 ms after PS_RDY, past the 310 ms default, and the hard
+		 * reset that followed stopped pass-through charging. The OnePlus
+		 * stack on Android waits 500 ms.
+		 */
+		sink-wait-cap-time-ms = <620>;
+
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
-- 
